# Upload rules for the Vercel build.
#
# Leading slashes anchor every pattern at the REPO ROOT. This matters: a bare
# `src/` (or `dist/`) also matches nested directories such as app/src/ and
# app/dist/, which silently stripped the new app's own sources from the upload
# and broke the build. Anchored patterns cannot do that.
#
# The frozen top-level src/ tree IS uploaded — it is small, and Vercel needs
# the repo layout intact. Only genuinely unused/heavy dirs are excluded here.
/frontend/
/docs/
/tests/
/scripts/
# root dist/ is the OLD app's build output — never shipped. Vercel rebuilds
# app/dist/ on its own machine and reads it as outputDirectory, so it is NOT
# ignored.
/dist/
/data/backups/
/data/raw/
/fullstack.md
# NOTE: no blanket *.md rule — api/report/latest.ts reads data/reports/publish-*.md
# from the deployed filesystem at runtime.
# .vercelignore replaces .gitignore for uploads — carry over the safety entries
.env*
.vercel_python_packages/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
validation_*.txt
*.log
